lgEUhwHNDQAbQgZmAACXJIyo+sqhCgAAAABJRU5ErkJgggs=</value></data><data name="LblCols.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Specify report columns and headers, as well as summaries to occur after the last  row of an old Sort column value or at the end of the report. You can reference columns in the old row by specifying the column bounded by {  and }. Double-click the "At Bottom of" Column header to choose the Sort Column</value></data>
  <data name="LblColSpan.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Column spanning generally occurs with pivoted data. E.g., Week1@Day1, Week1@Day2 are columns with two levels separated by character @ for Weeks and Days. The 2nd level header will be merged by Week Name</value></data>
  <data name="LblHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enter Report Header. Reference columns in first row of report by name bounded by {  and }. E.g., {StartDate}. Use &lt;DAY&gt; to display today's date, &lt;WW&gt; for Intel WW, &lt;DOW&gt; for Week Day, &lt;TS&gt; for current time, &lt;DOF&gt; for CSV File Date, and &lt;SP&gt; for a space</value></data>
  <data name="LblTopOf.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enter a subtitle to be written before the first row of a new sort column value. You can also reference columns in the new row by specifying the column name bounded by { and }. E.g., {Operation}. Double-click the "At Top of" row header to choose the Sort Column</value></data>
